workedExamples.solution_text:
The first $28^{\circ}$ south reaches the Equator. The rest of the journey continues into the Southern hemisphere.
[tikz]% mathsmap-diagram-colours {"version":1,"kind":"graph","base":[],"semantic":[],"reference":"template latitude-cross-equator-solution"}
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1mm,y=1mm]
\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes="1"/>}
\path[use as bounding box] (-6,-2.5) rectangle (102,15.8);
\draw[black,line width=0.5pt,<->] (-4,0)--(100,0);
\draw[black,line width=0.4pt] (0,-1.3)--(0,1.3);
\draw[black,line width=0.4pt] (8,-1.3)--(8,1.3);
\draw[black,line width=0.4pt] (16,-1.3)--(16,1.3);
\draw[black,line width=0.4pt] (24,-1.3)--(24,1.3);
\draw[black,line width=0.4pt] (32,-1.3)--(32,1.3);
\draw[black,line width=0.4pt] (40,-1.3)--(40,1.3);
\draw[black,line width=0.4pt] (48,-1.3)--(48,1.3);
\draw[black,line width=0.4pt] (56,-1.3)--(56,1.3);
\draw[black,line width=0.4pt] (64,-1.3)--(64,1.3);
\draw[black,line width=0.4pt] (72,-1.3)--(72,1.3);
\draw[black,line width=0.4pt] (80,-1.3)--(80,1.3);
\draw[black,line width=0.4pt] (88,-1.3)--(88,1.3);
\draw[black,line width=0.4pt] (96,-1.3)--(96,1.3);
\fill[black] (9.6,0) circle[radius=1];
\node[above,text=black] at (9.6,1.6) {$Final$};
\fill[black] (40,0) circle[radius=1];
\node[above,text=black] at (40,1.6) {$Equator$};
\fill[black] (84.8,0) circle[radius=1];
\node[above,text=black] at (84.8,1.6) {$28^{\circ}\mathrm{N}$};
\draw[black,line width=0.4pt,->] (84.8,1.8) .. controls (66,11.8) and (28.4,11.8) .. (9.6,1.8);
\node[above,text=black] at (47.2,9.3) {$47^{\circ}\text{ south}$};
\end{tikzpicture}[/tikz]
$\begin{aligned}\text{Remaining southward travel}&=47^{\circ}-28^{\circ}\\&=19^{\circ}\end{aligned}$
The final latitude is $19^{\circ}\text{S}$. Longitude stays $72^{\circ}\text{E}$, so the final coordinates are $(19^{\circ}\text{S},72^{\circ}\text{E})$.

